^SAMPLE = GSM9007959
!Sample_title = CRLM1_Colon_CD45+
!Sample_geo_accession = GSM9007959
!Sample_status = Public on Aug 11 2025
!Sample_submission_date = May 27 2025
!Sample_last_update_date = Aug 11 2025
!Sample_type = SRA
!Sample_channel_count = 1
!Sample_source_name_ch1 = Peritumoral Colon
!Sample_organism_ch1 = Homo sapiens
!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 9606
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = tissue: Peritumoral Colon
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = cell type: CD45+ TILs
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = run: 1
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = lane: 3
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = age: 39
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = Sex: Female
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = cytoplasmic RNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = The peritumoral colon and liver tissue samples were surgically sampled from tissue-area adjacent to the tumor mass. These were then chopped into small fragments, digested in HBSS+/+ containing 2 mg/ml of Collagenase Type I solution (Gibco), 2% FBS (Sigma Aldrich), 50 µg/ml DNAse I (Sigma Aldrich) and 10mM HEPES (Sigma-Aldrich), and subsequently incubated for 35 min at 37°C in the same solution. The resulting single-cell suspension was filtered through a 100 µm cell strainer and erythrocytes were lysed with BD Lysing Buffer. Cells were pelleted, counted, and frozen according to the slow freezing procedure in standard cryo-vials (1 ml cell suspension in the cryopreservation medium) and stored at -80 until use. Next, the cells were thawed, washed in PBS, stained with Live/dead Aqua Fluorescent Reactive Dye (Thermo Fisher Scientific) and mouse anti-human CD45 antibody 2D1 (BD Biosciences) at 4°C for 20 minutes and sorted by FACS Melody cell sorter (BD Biosciences). Freshly PBMCs were isolated through Lympholyte®-H Cell Separation density gradient solution (Cedarlane Laboratories) according to the manufacturer’s instructions and frozen in Fetal Bovine Serum (FBS, Sigma Aldrich) supplemented with 10% of the cryoprotective dimethyl sulfoxide (DMSO, PanReac AppliChem).
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Libraries for scRNA-seq were generated using a microfluidic-based approach on the Chromium Single-Cell Platform using the Chromium Single-Cell 5′ Library and Gel Bead Kit (10X Genomics, 1000006), according to the manufacturer’s instructions. In brief, thawed samples were evaluated for viability prior to scRNA-seq analysis, and all were ≥95% viable. Single cells were individually loaded onto a Chromium single-cell controller (10X Genomics) to generate single-cell gel beads-in-emulsion (GEMs). Captured cells were then lysed and the released RNA was barcoded through reverse transcription in individual GEMs. The concentration of the scRNA-seq libraries was assessed using an Agilent 4200 TapeStation system. The libraries were sequenced using an Illumina Novaseq6000 sequencer with a paired-end 150-bp (PE150) reading strategy (performed by CapitalBio Technology).
!Sample_description = Library name: CRLM1_Colon_CD45+
!Sample_description = 10x Genomics
!Sample_data_processing = Fastq files were processed with Cellranger v7.1.0 (10X Genomics), using default parameters. The scRNA-seq reads were aligned to the GRCh38 (version refdata-gex-GRCh38-2020-A, 10X Genomics) human genome reference. Only mapped reads with valid barcodes and unique molecular identifiers (UMIs) were retained to compute a gene expression matrix containing the number of UMI for every cell and gene.
!Sample_data_processing = Assembly: GRCh38 (version refdata-gex-GRCh38-2020-A, 10X Genomics)
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary files format and content: Matrix files in h5 format
!Sample_platform_id = GPL24676
